[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:The Best and the Worst]
[00:03.69]The best and the worst
[00:08.28]First listen and then answer the question.
[00:14.65]Why is Joe's garden the most beautiful one in the town?
[00:22.32]Joe Sanders has the most beautiful garden in our town.
[00:28.22]Nearly everybody enters for 'The Nicest Garden Competition' each year, but Joe wins every time.
[00:38.46]Bill Frith's garden is larger than Joe's.
[00:42.45]Bill works harder than Joe and grows more flowers and vegetables, but Joe's garden is more interesting.
[00:51.85]He has made neat paths and has built a wooden bridge over a pool.
[00:58.49]I like gardens too, but I do not like hard work.
[01:04.45]Every year I enter for the garden competition too, and I always win a little prize for the worst garden in the town!
